### 18.1 What the cases can establish

These experiments distinguish application from contribution: a procedure can be exercised, reconstruct a feasible option and tie ordinary analysis. A final choice can differ while its mechanism already exists in a proposal or criticism. Fixed-pool selection does not establish generation. The closed cases disclose supported affordances and permit strong ordinary controls to attain modeled workload floors; a local tie cannot establish that creativity has no value in less explicit settings. Per-card findings and their available comparison evidence are retained in the linked report.

The first missing-output ordinary calls and invalid cap-bound builders remain failed observations, with their gates and unavailable contrasts. Fresh controls supply later evidence. The original example-free builder saved no JSON after using an unavailable interpreter command; its later endpoint uses the unchanged valid original critique and preserves that first failure. After 61 original roles had finished, 132 still-unadmitted packets received an explicit one-candidate builder/transfer field matching the existing validator; compliance across these two phases is not a creativity or learning effect. Later reviewers also received actual assigned input envelopes and literal case/method packs.

Two later COV-REVIEW-1 draws added prohibited fields and remain invalid. Their raw rows are explicitly marked as unadmitted assessments. A prospective review-literal clarification made the existing six-key schema explicit for eight still-unadmitted later reviews and two conditional grammar reviews, preserving all prior packets, schemas, validators and grades. This addresses a conflicting general empty-field instruction; it is a protocol limitation and compliance clarification, not a creativity or learning effect.

The initial later75-role protocol remains intact. Five separately admitted later roles add an older matched-absence endpoint and four fresh reviews, giving an80-disposition subtotal before source coverage. The failed first matched-absence builder omitted job_id and reported a generic memory lookup before reading its packet. Its unused-results claim is unverified. The new endpoint uses the unchanged valid critique without the failed builder output; the first failure remains visible. Explicit existing key sets and task-first source instructions are disclosed protocol clarity, not a learning effect.

A pure review-start assertion failed before admission or native call when it counted historical instruction copies within the evidence payload. The frozen current-envelope wrapper preserves those source bytes and clarifies only the active instruction. This is an adapter correction, not a native retry or strategy result. The grammar preparation inherited stale260 budget wording; its prospectively frozen memo supersedes that wording only with the actual later cumulative300 ceiling, preserving originalroot260.

Four pre-clarification source-route draws added prohibited provenance/pool fields and remain invalid, with four uncalled descendants. The prospective complete-key instruction names the existing13 keys and puts source detail in existing traces/handoffs. A separate ten-role comparison supplies fresh shared/distinct chains and two reviews, reusing valid pre-assistance pools rather than rerunning them. Aggregate later coverage is75+5+10=90 dispositions; all three plans remain distinct. The ten-role v17 plan prospectively supersedes the unadmitted six-role v16 preparation, not sixteen executions. Other invalid source arms stay unavailable. The preserved preparation budget note identifies duplicate grammar reservation in an unrun estimate; actual admission uses the recomputed live300 ceiling.

Actual paired source reviews then identified missing full precursor arrays and provenance in selected exchange summaries. Eight separately admitted v18 roles execute three fresh exchanges, three summary-only builders and two independent reviews. Exchanges receive a root-frozen literal preservation capsule; builders receive it only through the actual selected summary. All six exchange/builder roles have an explicitly larger10000-word transmission cap, versus earlier1800. The unchanged precursor/route stages are reused; this is literal handoff coverage, not a matched efficacy or equal-compute experiment. Earlier incomplete summaries and grades remain visible. Actual transmission checks are recorded in [provenance verification](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/runs/2026-10-10-academic-twenty/reports/PROVENANCE-FIDELITY-VERIFICATION.v1.json). All three new builders choose a known two-action clip, compared with earlier six-action head-loop SHARED/DISTINCT and six-action stem-sleeve UNION endpoints. Larger aided handoffs confound that comparison: it is no isolated method effect, invention or compression-efficiency proof. The actual fresh ordinary reference already used two active actions; the new reconstructions recover that workload floor. Later coverage is75+5+10+8=98; with original197 and grammar14, there were309 admitted scheduled dispositions before N08 coverage. The prospectively frozen v2 root-owned ceiling310 follows preserved260 and300 protocols; the user-authorized native goal is unbudgeted.

The first completion auditors disagreed on primary older-method coverage for AC04: A blocked while B passed. Original T/N08 counts3/2 and later methodO ordering counts3/3 remain separate. Five prospective v19 roles add a fresh N:N08 proposal, critique/Distill, summary-only builder and two independent AC04 reviews. The unchanged valid later T chain is reused; J0 facts/components/topologies, common source bank, three initial candidates, six declared slots and1800-word construction-stage caps match. Named-interface crossing and interaction prediction supply the missing earlier-method operation. Counts/caps do not certify equal effort or invention. Both first audit outputs remain unchanged. Aggregate later coverage is103; original197+later103+grammar14 totals314 scheduled dispositions. Two additional completion audits were separately reserved within the unchanged310 ceiling. A pure closure-only preflight assertion rejected the five pending roles before admission; source integrity passed and no native call resulted.

### 18.2 Learning and emergence

The academic evidence supports conditional improvements in creative performance through training. This agent study instead investigates mechanisms and external procedures. Context availability is not human incubation; retrieved cards are not unassisted retention; one-field external revision is not weight training. Actual beneficiary preferences support a usefulness question, while synthetic action counts do not measure beneficiary relief. Different routed source packs establish an information intervention, not independent empirical discoveries.

No universal necessary-and-sufficient recipe emerges. For this research process, useful novelty requires usable knowledge, an admissible variable, actual construction, comparison with existing work and purpose-relevant evaluation. Retention and unfamiliar-case transfer require further evidence when learning is claimed. The eight [next experiment proposals](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/runs/2026-10-10-academic-twenty/reports/INTERPRETATION-NOTES.v1.md) investigate discovery costs, explicit grammar, matched ordering, state-bearing learning, transferable feedback, constructive attack, beneficiary outcomes and equal-information source diversity. They remain proposals.

### 18.3 Closeout and persistence

The final study used **308 actual native invocation attempts** within its separately frozen310-call later cumulative ceiling; original260 and previous later300 root protocols remain preserved. All admitted dispositions are terminal and both new completion auditors pass essential agent execution and comparison coverage. Historical raw evidence and all first assessments remain intact. The catalog, source register, external procedure artifacts and execution evidence persist in the project; they have not been installed as global skills or changed defaults.

[Final accounting and audit evidence](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/runs/2026-10-10-academic-twenty/reports/RESULTS.v5.json) records actual invocation and source checks. Aggregate goal token/time usage is a timestamped bookkeeping snapshot; per-role tokens, hidden compute and hardware costs are unavailable. Native terminal events are root/coordinator observations, without independent platform authentication.

## 19. Rhetoric, contradictions and the strategy-game case

The 11 October extension brings irony, sarcasm, surprise, contradictions and indirection into the novelty investigation, using the user's strategy game as a concrete design case. The user clarified **contradictions**, and a roster of **three characters from which the player deploys one**. The deployed hero must survive **three stages, each with a boss**, acquiring items and improving skills during the run. Manual play should reward execution within a strategy; autoplay should reward authored planning. These are the preserved design constraints, not measured outcomes.

### 19.1 Research and prepared strategies

The initial phase of the [new research report](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/RESEARCH-AND-GAME-DESIGN.md) added **nine academic references** around sarcasm, irony, schema violations, pragmatics and game mechanisms; the subsequent principles phase adds seven more, described in section 19.5. Source access depth varies: targeted paper passages and primary abstracts support scoped claims; two scanned chapters are explicitly limited to context/bibliography rather than full-text review. A source finding or framework is not evidence that this workflow or game improves creativity.

[Fourteen additional strategy cards, RT01–RT14](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/RHETORICAL-STRATEGIES.md) operationalize the directions: echo a failed promise; sarcastic praise followed by literal reconstruction; prediction-led surprise; contradictions resolved through time or space; reversal of outcome value; acting through an opponent's goal; converting residue; teaching and betraying a pattern; abstention; expressive input; countering a build's assumption; meaning reconstruction; and obligation-preserving distillation after attack. Each card includes a construction, a control and a defeating observation. **These strategies are prepared, not efficacy-tested.** Their IDs do not replace or regrade AC01–AC20.

A [seventeen-game precedent map](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/GAME-PRECEDENTS.md) establishes documented overlap for maze planning, direct combat, automated builds, authored behavior, systemic effects, rule manipulation, voice input and rhythm-linked combat, plus Goat Simulator as a contrasting experience case. Official descriptions and attributed creator testimony were researched; the games were not played in this extension. Absence from a description is not evidence of absence from the game or the wider market. No completely new mechanic is certified.

### 19.2 Concrete design and unusual constructions

The [game design](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/GAME-DESIGN.md) proposes Bastion for guarded contact/retaliation, Mason for temporary mazes and routing, and Veil for mobile magic/poison. Shared world/action contracts support manual commands or a bounded player-authored policy. The three boss stages pressure different enabling assumptions while preserving usable build windows. Lethal terrain requires advance warning and a temporally reachable escape at issuance; subsequent voluntary mistakes can still lose that escape.

The unusual starting operation is a scarce response bound to an enemy's public objective: touch the hero, wound the hero, or reach a seal. Guarded contact can fulfill touch while defeating direct wound; interception can defeat arrival at a health/resource cost. Catalyst spending, empowerment, cancellation, death, payoff storage and direct-damage endpoints are explicit. Worked utility examples show possible goal-dependent action rankings under their declared assumptions; they were not played or simulated. A conventional reward keyed to the same objective can reproduce the operation, so the defensible distinction is against named goal-independent controls, not all ordinary game effects.

A [portfolio of twenty-four proposed mechanics](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/WILD-MECHANICS.md) preserves the wider creative space: empowered charges, overgrown healed armor, enemy paths drawing spells, destructive walls as batteries, visible enemy memory, singing and silence. Singing quality is narrowly defined as calibrated pitch/rhythm conformity with a bounded effect and an alternative input; musical beauty is not inferred. Sound remains a separate input study, not a required dependency of the starting run.

### 19.3 Actual design process and evidence boundary

The [Distill result](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/DISTILL-RESULT.md) records **two actual subagents, two tracks, three proposal/critique rounds and six completed role turns**. Named objections changed command disposition, route authority, hazard responsibility, catalyst economics, event ordering, token lifecycle, endpoint semantics and comparison controls. Both final design-contract assessments pass under the declared candidate assumptions; overall readiness remains **flag** for implementation, feel, usability, balance, enjoyment, strategic advantage, learning and broader originality. The requested design study is complete at its three-round boundary.

Canonical Robot Talks was not executed in this extension. It remains a possible later cross-layer route with its own applicability conditions. The [descriptive dispatch](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/RESEARCH-DISPATCH.json) uses the sibling domainspec-core Dispatch Spec validator. The initial shape error and subsequent passing validation are preserved in the dated package. Shape validation does not verify a playable game or confer canonical skill authority.

[Validation and navigation](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/VALIDATION.md) records local artifact checks. Future goal-pair, authoring, gameplay and delayed-transfer probes remain unrun. The catalogs and research persist as repository-local preparations; no global skill or default was installed. Earlier experimental artifacts, findings and invocation denominators remain unchanged; the six design turns belong only to this new scope.

### 19.4 Goat Simulator: unexpected premise and experience

The user added *Goat Simulator* as an example of a game that attracted unexpected attention. The [case study](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/GOAT-SIMULATOR-CASE.md) covers the original 2014 game and links the official description with two attributed developer accounts. Westbergh's launch-period interview describes prototype-video interest influencing the decision to release it. This is reported development history, rather than an audited causal explanation of popularity. [Developer interview](https://www.gamedeveloper.com/business/q-a-the-weird-wacky-success-that-is-i-goat-simulator-i-).

The research interpretation is that novelty can change **what an experience is for and what makes it valuable**, alongside changing a feasible decision. Investigate ironic expectations, absurd premises, recoverable failure and retellable consequences. Familiar mechanics can carry a surprising experience; finding an ordinary mechanical equivalent does not settle that separate claim. Audience expectations, enjoyment and sustained appeal need their own comparisons.

Six case-derived prompts and four proposed comparisons transfer this direction into the strategy game. They preserve the one-character expedition and its legible costs and hazards. The seventeen-game source register now includes GP17 and its two supporting creator accounts. This addition follows the completed design dialogue; it contributes no new role turns, scored gameplay results or efficacy findings.

### 19.5 General principles and applicability of irony and sarcasm

The user's clarification makes the underlying principles and their applicability the target, with game design as one application. The [principles report](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/PRINCIPLES-AND-APPLICABILITY.md) distinguishes what an ironic act communicates, how its meaning is understood, whether it affects creative performance and whether a deliberate method transfers. Echoic and pretense accounts explain different aspects of the act; salience and cue-integration accounts concern processing. These are competing or differently scoped explanations, rather than a settled universal mechanism.

The working transfer hypothesis is to make an attributed expectation and its relation to evidence visible, reconsider the representation or success criterion, then construct and compare an alternative. Eight proposed principles address belief representation, competing interpretations, evaluative criteria, abstraction, scoped tensions, context, social delivery and constructive comparison. Applicability is mapped across individual reasoning, product metrics, architecture, research inquiry, collaboration, teaching, communication, AI-assisted investigation and precise instructions.

The [ten PR strategies](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/PRINCIPLE-STRATEGIES.md) provide constructions and defeating comparisons beyond games. They are adaptations with acknowledged overlap with established practices. A worked support-metric example converts an ironic description into distinct resolution states and outcome checks; it is authored illustration, not an observed organizational result.

Seven references, AR10–AR16, brought the dated extension to sixteen academic entries at this phase. Nemeth et al., A17 from the earlier academic extension, is reused without another count. The proposed comparison separates ordinary analysis, literal expectation contrast, irony, sarcasm, direct abstraction and conflicting-requirement integration, with the same facts and constructive obligation. Method benefit, perceived hostility, engagement, comprehension and delayed transfer remain separate outcomes. These studies are prepared and unrun; human comprehension findings establish no internal mechanism for an AI agent.

### 19.6 Strategies for generating game mechanics

The game research now explicitly includes **methods for inventing mechanics**, alongside the game that invites players to invent strategies. The [sixteen MG cards](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/MECHANIC-GENERATION-STRATEGIES.md) transform seeds by reversing benefits, retaining failure residue, changing action ownership, coupling liabilities, partitioning contradictions, making information contestable, shaping expectations, exchanging geometry, importing expressive input, withholding actions, borrowing causal relations, removing staples, reconstructing after attack, mutating a typed rule and making absurd premises playable. Each provides an example and a comparison that could defeat a novelty claim. These are prepared adaptations, not sixteen certified new methods.

The [four worked constructions](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/MECHANIC-GENERATION-EXAMPLES.md) compose these operators into MC01–MC04: a song sets the next enemy combo's rhythm; a barricade opens another passage; injury positions draw temporary routing geometry; an item connects an eligible event to an effect. The written proposals specify costs, state transitions, feedback, manual/autoplay demands, counters and conventional equivalents. They add candidates to the portfolio without rewriting the base expedition or its twenty-four WM entries.

AR17 and AR18 add primary generation precedents: restricted mechanic/level search in [*Mechanic Miner* (Cook et al., 2013)](https://soundandcomplete.org/papers/EVO2013/MechanicMiner-EvoGames-2013.pdf), and composable actions with modeled playability checks in [*Automatic Game Design via Mechanic Generation* (Zook & Riedl, inspected 2019 preprint)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.01420). Neither was run locally. The dated source register now contains eighteen academic entries and seventeen games; the earlier twenty-six-reference register retains its separate scope.

The [construction record](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/MECHANIC-GENERATION-TRACE.json) is authored documentation of transformations and checks, not independent review or observed play. No new agent turns, experiments, simulation or gameplay results are added. Future comparisons should separately assess whether the methods improve generation, whether the resulting mechanics create valuable play, and whether players learn transferable creativity.


### 19.7 Composing generators and checking existing mechanics

The completed follow-up treats **mechanic invention as the research output**, using the proposed game as a test case. Six ordered MG combinations generate eighteen initial drafts: a representative, unusual reserve and provisional rejection per combination. Six representatives are subsequently refined without inflating the draft count. The [full study report](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/composition-study-001/REPORT.md) connects the recipes to irony, scoped contradiction, indirection, attack-to-reconstruct and absurd purpose; [twelve reusable investigation rules](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/composition-study-001/METHOD-LESSONS.md) carry the findings beyond the case.

Three actual Robot Talks investigators completed fifteen findings across rules, control/authorship and player interpretation. The human approved setup and accepted all six [synthesis dispositions](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/composition-study-001/ROBOT-TALKS-SYNTHESIS.md). These obligations concern commitment/safety compatibility, usable information windows, six-rule policies, attack withholding, capped benefit and reserve deferral. Both gates are fulfilled.

Every C01–C06 completes the retained three proposal/critique/reconciliation conversations. **Twelve actual role turns** comprise G0 construction, eight Distill proposal/critique turns and three Robot Talks investigations. Parent reconciliation and historical design turns are excluded. Eight actual packs supply eighty-eight technique rows. The original cap fires; [final Distill Result](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/composition-study-001/DISTILL-RESULT.md) records the dependency-bearing action card as the smallest coherent unit, its recomposition and deferred next route.

The [final independent critique](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/composition-study-001/BALANCER-R3.md) closes all five round-two repairs in the bounded written scope, with no new concrete blocker raised. All six contracts have scoped written closure under authored assumptions and an overall **flag** for untested feasibility, usefulness, comprehension and novelty. Original independent blocks remain attached to earlier versions; [root reconciliation](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/composition-study-001/RECONCILIATION-R3.md) does not rewrite those receipts. C05-V2's undefined protection liability remains unpromoted.

The follow-up source set contains twenty-five game entries and twenty-eight primary records, including two additional Valve abilities within the existing Dota entry. [Final operation comparisons](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/composition-study-001/COMPARISONS-FINAL.md) identify familiar ingredients and narrower relations. C02 explicitly distinguishes cast-origin histories at equal final position. C04 retains a compulsory vector while changing its settlement origin through attack restraint. These are prioritized discrimination questions, not established worldwide inventions.

Two limiting findings are retained. C03's ordered bend has a different literal trajectory, while competent straight east reproduces the same E-zone memory response in its paired toy case. C06's current gate law and stale enemy route can be reproduced by an inspected-and-cached route system; version labels add no demonstrated mechanical primitive. The Goat Simulator lens separately preserves novelty of purpose and experience when mechanical relations are familiar. No singing-quality scoring, sarcasm-induced creativity, learned enemy model or audience-surprise result is inferred.

The [completion audit](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/composition-study-001/COMPLETION-AUDIT.md), [exact trace](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/composition-study-001/DISTILL-TRACE.json) and [artifact validation](/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/rhetoric-game-design/2026-10-11/composition-study-001/VALIDATION.md) document the fulfilled paper scope. Earlier twenty-nine snapshot files, fourteen frozen inputs and the original sections 1–18 are preserved. No game implementation, simulation, gameplay, publication, global skill/default change or human creativity-training experiment was performed. A later matched method, prototype or audience study is a separately scoped investigation.
